quran[25]{c,v,t}:
  78,31,"For the God-conscious, there will indeed be success,"
  78,32,"(in the form of) gardens and vineyards,"
  78,33,"and full-bosomed maidens of matching age,"
  78,34,and overflowing cups (of pure wine).
  78,35,"They will not hear therein any vain talk nor lying,"
  78,36,"as a reward from your Lord, a generously befitting bestowal (in proportion to your works),"
  78,37,"(from) the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, the Most-Compassionate (Lord), whom they will not be able to address,"
  78,38,on the Day when the Holy Spirit and the angels stand in rows. They will not speak except whom the Most-Compassionate (Lord) permits and who says what is right.
  78,39,"That is the True Day. So whosoever wishes, let him take the path leading back to his Lord."
  78,40,"We have indeed warned you of an imminent punishment on the Day when (every) person will see what his hands have sent forth, and the disbeliever will say: ‘Oh, I wish if only I had been dust!’"
  79,1,"By (the angels) who snatch (the evil souls) violently,*"
  79,2,"and by (the angels) who draw out (the blessed souls) gently,*"
  79,3,"and by (the angels) who float (in space) swiftly,*"
  79,4,"and by (the angels) who take the lead, racing vigorously,*"
  79,5,and then by (the angels) who manage the affairs (of creatures obediently).*
  79,6,"The Day when the quaking Blast quakes violently,"
  79,7,"the succeeding Blast will follow it,"
  79,8,"the hearts on that Day will be trembling (in horror),"
  79,9,their eyes will be downcast (bearing a terrified look).
  79,10,"They (the disbelievers) say: ‘Will we surely be returned to our earlier state,"
  79,11,even after we have become decayed bones?’
  79,12,"They say: ‘Then, this will be a (great) losing return.’"
  79,13,Yet it will be only a single Mighty Blast.
  79,14,"And behold! Suddenly, they will be upon the vast expanse (of the Day of Resurrection)."
  79,15,Has the story of Musa (Moses) reached you?
